{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And now, sons, listen to me</b> — language of conciliation." "<b>And happy are those who keep my ways</b> — language of intensification. The sense of 'my ways' is like the sense of 'and I will make known to them the way in which they shall walk' (Exodus 33:13 [the verse reads 'the way' rather than 'my ways'; the comparison may be to a different verse or reflect Ibn Ezra's paraphrase])."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:35.091007160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}